        <p class="timeline-org">Max Planck Institute for Human Cognition and Brain Sciences & University of Gießen</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Researching NeuroAI approaches for efficient experimental design in visual neuroscience: using modern computer vision models and large-scale naturalistic image spaces to choose better stimuli, compare model and brain representations, and improve fMRI dataset coverage. Built the ML/data infrastructure behind these workflows, including public datasets and <a href="https://re-vision-initiative.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">re:vision</a> challenge infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p class="timeline-tech">Python · PyTorch · CLIP · scikit-learn · SLURM · Docker</p>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item timeline-item--research">
        <div class="timeline-meta">
          <span class="timeline-date">Jun 2021 - May 2022</span>
          <span class="timeline-kind">Research</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Research Assistant - ML in Medicine</h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">ScaDS.AI Dresden/Leipzig</p>
        <p class="timeline-description">
          Engineered a multi-plane UNet++ ensemble for Glioblastoma segmentation (BraTS 2021), reaching 0.90 Dice for whole tumor. Developed attention-based mortality prediction models with epistemic uncertainty estimation.
        </p>
        <p class="timeline-tech">PyTorch · FT-Transformer · SAINT · UNet++</p>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item timeline-item--industry">
        <div class="timeline-meta">
          <span class="timeline-date">Oct 2019 - May 2021</span>
          <span class="timeline-kind">Industry</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="timeline-title">Data Scientist / ML Engineer <span class="role-meta">(Working student)</span></h3>
        <p class="timeline-org">CHECK24 (Travel Vertical)</p>
